  body: "# Retirement Pension contribution-record dispute\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe Category A section
    distinguishes a presumed-correct national insurance record from a disputed record requiring an HMRC formal decision,
    and the awards section describes incomplete-record handling.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDo not infer that
    a missing contribution record proves there is no entitlement. The source describes obtaining the complete record
    and reconsidering an initial decision, but no real claimant’s record is examined here.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 75032, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 75711, PDF page 160](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=160).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch75` — PDF SHA-256 `655e7acb31f09f5169efbe40419091ee479f88c0c45b65c7a507b042b67712f9`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `0d037880d2aeaff1be89235ee987ca4acb1c839fcf1ead8b8be2daa9f6795465`.\n- `dmg-vol12-ch74` — PDF SHA-256
    `5961a9cb7c86814a0f6fa147c0a8a551b4258c803680fac14a95cab9eca1afd6`; page-extraction SHA-256 `c762e93940b4342d70d5bc96a80c3e094c91852d93868f5709e04f293faef61a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source says an initial decision based on incomplete contribution information is to be
      revised when complete information becomes available.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch75/0160
      quote: "75711 If the conditions of entitlement are satisfied the DM should make an award of RP. However, the\n\
        DM will sometimes be unable to obtain the claimant’s complete contribution record for the period up to\n\
        the year before that in which entitlement occurs. In this event the DM should\n\n\n1. make an initial decision
        based on the information held and\n\n\n2. commence action immediately to obtain the complete record and\n\
        \n\n3. revise the initial decision when the complete information is available.\n\n\nThe DM may require HMRC
        to decide the contribution issue."
      locator: DMG 75711
  - target: term/sp-contribution-record-dispute
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The two chapters both explicitly route disputes about NI contribution records to HMRC; this
      association does not make their underlying benefit conditions equivalent.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch75/0010
      quote: "75032 Entitlement to Cat A RP depends on the contribution conditions being satisfied. In practice
        the NI\ncontribution record is usually obtained and any decision is based on the assumption that the record
        is\nfactually correct. However, where there is a dispute about the record, the matter must be referred by
        the\n\nDM to HMRC for a formal decision1. That referral should be made2 to:\nHMRC\nNational Insurance Contributions
        Office\nNE98 1ZZ\n\n\nNote 1: See DMG Chapters 03, 04 and 06 for guidance on how decisions and appeals are
        handled after a\nreference to HMRC.\n\n\nNote 2: See DMG Chapter 01 where the dispute is about whether credits
        should be awarded.\n\n\n     1 SS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 11A and 38A; 2 Secretary of State for Work and Pensions
        v TB v HMRC (RP)\n                                                                                     \
        \                    [2010]\n                                                                          \
        \   UKUT 88 (AAC) [2010] AACR 38"
      locator: DMG 75032
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0003
      quote: "74012 Entitlement to SP at any of the rates in DMG 74011 depends on the conditions of entitlement\n\
        being satisfied. In practice the NI contribution record is usually obtained and any decision is based on
        the\nassumption that the record is factually correct. However, where there is a dispute about the record,
        the\n\nmatter must be referred by the DM to HMRC for a formal decision1. That referral should be made2 to:\n\
        HMRC\nNational Insurance Contributions Office\nNE98 1ZZ\n\n\nNote 1: See DMG Chapters 03, 04 and 06 for
        guidance on how decisions and appeals are handled after a\nreference to HMRC.\n\n\nNote 2: See DMG Chapter
        01 where the dispute is about whether credits should be awarded.\n\n\n                        1 SS CS (D&A)
        Regs, reg 11A and 38A; 2 Secretary of State for Work and Pensions\n                                    \
        \            v TB v HMRC (RP) [2010} UKUT 88 (AAC) [2010] AACR 38"
      locator: DMG 74012
